      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3.6v+21.6=0 \\\\ 3v+4w+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3.6v+21.6=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 3v+4w+2=0 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}36v+216=0 \\\\ 3v+4w+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can easily solve for $v$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36v+216 & =0 \\\\ 36v & =-216 \\\\ v & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $w,$ we can substitute $v=-6$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3v+4w+2 & =0 \\\\ 3(-6)+4w+2 & =0 \\\\ -18+4w+2 & =0 \\\\ 4w & =16 \\\\ w & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=-6,\\,w=4.$",
