      "dom_id": "question-18760",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Let $(a,b)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.05a-0.2b=0.04 \\\\ 0.12a-1.2b=0.24\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.05a-0.2b=0.04 & |\\times 100 \\\\ 0.12a-1.2b=0.24 & |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5a-20b=4 \\\\ 12a-120b=24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and divide the second equation by $3,$ we will get a $40b$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-40b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5a-20b=4 & |\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 12a-120b=24 & |\\,÷3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-10a+40b=-8 \\\\ 4a-40b=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable and allows us to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10a+\\cancel{40b} & =-8 \\\\ 4a-\\cancel{40b} & =8 \\\\ (-10a+4a) & =(-8+8) \\\\ -6a & =0 \\\\ a & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=0$ into the equation $5a-20b=4$ to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-20b & =4 \\\\ 5(0)-20b & =4 \\\\ -20b & =4 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ b & =-0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=0,\\,b=-0.2.$ So,\n\n$$\na+b=0+(-0.2)=-0.2.\n$$",
